<title>ITALY: MOTOR RACING-FRENTZEN WINS SAN MARINO GRAND PRIX.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-FRENTZEN WINS SAN MARINO GRAND PRIX.</headline>
<dateline>IMOLA, Italy 1997-04-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Heinz-Harald Frentzen of</p>
<p>Germany, driving a Williams, won the San Marino Grand Prix motor</p>
<p>race on Sunday.</p>
<p>Michael Schumacher of Germany was second in a Ferrari with</p>
<p>Britain's Eddie Irvine also in a Ferrari third.</p>
<p>Giancarlo Fisichella of Italy finished fourth in a Jordan,</p>
<p>with Jean Alesi of France in a Benetton fifth and Finland's Mika</p>
<p>Hakkinen sixth in a McLaren.</p>
<p>World drivers' championship standings (after four rounds):</p>
<p> 1. Villeneuve				    20 points</p>
<p> 2. Michael Schumacher (Germany)	    14</p>
<p> 3. equal Heinz-Harald Frentzen (Germany) 10</p>
<p> 3. equal.David Coulthard (Britain)	 10</p>
<p> 3. equal Eddie Irvine (Britain)	    10</p>
<p> 3. equal.Gerhard Berger  (Austria)	 10</p>
<p> 3. equal Mika Hakkinen (Finland)	   10</p>
<p> 8  Oliver Panis (France)			6</p>
<p> 9. Ralf Schumacher				4</p>
<p> 10 equal Giancarlo Fisichella (Italy)     3</p>
<p> 10.equal Johnny Herbert (Britain)	   3</p>
<p> 10 equal. Jean Alesi (France)		 3</p>
<p> 13.Nicola Larini (Italy)			1</p>
<p>Constructors' championship:</p>
<p> 1. Williams				  30 points</p>
<p> 2. Ferrari				   24</p>
<p> 3. McLaren-Mercedes			20</p>
<p> 4. Benetton-Renault			13</p>
<p> 6  Jordan				     7</p>
<p> 5. Prost					6</p>
<p> 6  Sauber-Petronas			  4</p>
</text>
